cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, cite it as below."
title: "agent-faultbench: does an agent's defence actually stop an action that should not run?"
abstract: >-
  A conformance suite for agent failure modes. The judged question is the gap
  between what an agent reports it did and what actually happened on disk. v0.3.0
  covers truncated tool calls and carries three imported suites (double-exec, cutoff, runaway); expected values are read from a git ref, and the evidence is the file on disk, not a log line.
authors:
  - family-names: Yuan
    given-names: Simin
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/simin-yuan/agent-faultbench"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords:
  - agents
  - benchmark
  - reliability
  - fault-injection
  - tool-calling
  - evaluation
